
# Cloudflare Workers HTTP transport. Unlike the node transport (which binds a socket via hono +
# @hono/node-server), a Worker never listens: `serve` returns a Web-standard fetch handler and the
# Workers runtime invokes it per request. The `<global:transport>` shim's `create-fetch` wraps the
# uniform router (`handle-request`) in that handler; the matching + dispatch stay in the
# platform-agnostic `handle-request`, exactly as on node. The emitted Worker entry re-exports the
# returned handler as `export default`.

dock load
  load <global:transport>, name runtime
  note native

load ../../http
  find server
  find request
  find response
  find handle-request

task serve
  take server, like server
  take port, like u16

  send back
    call runtime/create-fetch
      bind handle
        task on-request
          take incoming, like request
          like response
          send back
            call handle-request
              read server
              read incoming
